    <!-- ================= DECORATION =================
         WHAT IS DOWN HERE AND WHY IT CANNOT MOVE A FIELD.

         The owner's first note on the M6 recording was that the hall
         looks empty. It is: twelve rack segments and an annex in
         48 x 32 m read as a test track rather than a factory. So the
         floor is dressed - and dressed in the two places the safety
         layer physically cannot see.

         The three microScan3 fans and the nav lidar are HORIZONTAL and
         are mounted between 0.30 and 1.50 m. The overhead camera looks
         straight DOWN from 38 m. Everything below therefore sits either
         ON TOP of an obstacle box (z >= 4.00) or FLAT on the floor
         (z = 0.005), and no scanner ray can reach either. Nothing here
         has a <collision>, nothing appears in stations.OBSTACLES, and
         nothing extends past the footprint of a rectangle that is
         already there.

         WHAT WAS NOT DONE, AND IT IS THE REASON THIS FILE IS DULL AT
         EYE LEVEL. The obvious way to make racking look like racking is
         to replace each solid box with uprights and beams. gpu_lidar
         renders VISUALS, so the gaps between those uprights would let a
         scanner see THROUGH racking it currently cannot, and every
         standoff measured against that racking would stop meaning what
         it says. The boxes are untouched. -->
